                  <summary/>
                  
                 
                  <msItem xml:id="ms_i1">
                     <locus from="2ra" to="149ra"/>
                     <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi">ʾAragāwi manfasāwi</title>
                     
                     <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.1">
                        <locus from="2ra" to="91vb"/>
                        <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi#Homilies">ʾAragāwi manfasāwi: 30 Homilies or treatises</title>
                        <note>There are 33 homilies. The numbers of <foreign xml:lang="gez">dǝrsānāt</foreign> (till 20) are written either in the margin or
                           in a separate line that precedes the title. Sometimes the numbers are rubricated.</note>
                     </msItem>
                     
                     <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.2">
                        <locus from="92ra" to="136rb"/>
                        <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi#Letters">ʾAragāwi manfasāwi: Epistles</title>
                        <note>There are 47 Letters.</note>
                        
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.2.1">
                           <locus from="92ra" to="94va"/>
                           <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi#Letters">
                              Epistles of ʾAragāwi Manfasāwi (malʾǝktāt): 2 letters</title>
                        </msItem>
                        <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.2.2">
                           <locus from="94va" to="136rb"/>
                           <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi#Letters">
                              Response letters  (fǝnnāwe malʾǝktāt): 45 letters</title>
                           
                           <note>From the third epistle onwards all the epistles (46) are marked as <foreign xml:lang="gez">fǝnnāwe malʾǝkt</foreign>. 
                              In <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdd036">Bǝḥerāwi Kǝllǝlāwi Mangǝśti Tǝgrāy, Dabra Dāmmo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi, C3-IV-251</ref>, 29 epistles are marked as <foreign xml:lang="gez">fǝnnāwe malʾǝktāt</foreign> as opposed
                              to 20 epistles marked as <foreign xml:lang="gez">malʾǝktāt</foreign>. <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm001">Gāntā ʾAfašum, Maḵodʿa Dabra Gannat Kidāna Mǝḥrat, GKM-001</ref> and <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESmakm012">ʾƎndartā, Māy ʾAnbasā Dabra Gannat Kidāna Mǝḥrat, MAKM-012</ref> contain 28 
                              <foreign xml:lang="gez">fǝnnāwe malʾǝktāt</foreign> as opposed to 22 <foreign xml:lang="gez">malʾǝktāt</foreign>. Despite the difference in naming, the
                              contents of the first 22 epistles in the present manuscript correspond to the first 22 <foreign xml:lang="gez">malʾǝktāt</foreign> in other manuscripts.</note>
                        </msItem>
                     </msItem>
                     
                     <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.3">
                        <locus from="136rb" to="147vb"/>
                        <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi#ChaptersKnowledge">ʾAragāwi manfasāwi: Compendium of three
        homilies on the spiritual life / Dǝrsān baʾǝnta ʾarʾǝsta ʾaʾǝmro</title>
                     </msItem>
                     
                     <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.4">
                        <locus from="148ra" to="148rb"/>
                        <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi#LetterExplanation">ʾAragāwi manfasāwi: Letter by John Saba to a
        monk called John</title>
                        
                     </msItem>
                     <msItem xml:id="ms_i1.5">
                        <locus from="148rb" to="149ra"/>
                        <title type="complete" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT3989Aragawi#AnswerExplanation">ʾAragāwi manfasāwi: Answer from the monk John
        to John Saba</title>
                     </msItem>
                     
                     <explicit type="embedded" xml:lang="gez" corresp="LIT3989Aragawi#NoteTranslationExplicit">
                        <locus target="#149ra"/> <hi rend="rubric">ተተርጐመ፡ ዝንቱ፡ መጽሐፍ፡ እምልሳነ፡ ዓረቢ፡ ኀበ፡
                        ልሳነ፡ ግዕዝ፡ ሐዲስ፡ በ</hi>ትእዛዘ፡ ቃሉ፡ ለልብነ፡ ድንግል፡ ንጉሥ፡ እምቃለ፡ ኑዛዜ፡ እንተ፡ ዘአረጋዊ፡ መንፈሳዊ፡
                        ዘጸሐፈ፡ በእንተ፡ አእምሮተ፡ እግዚአብሔር፨ ወምሥጢረ፡ ዓለም፡ ሐዲስ፡ ወበእንተ፡ ሀብታት፡ አምላካውያት፡ ወሕዋፄ፡ ጸጋ፡
                        እንተ፡ ይፌንዋ፡ ሎሙ፡ ለእለ፡ ያፈቅርዎ፡ ለፍቁራኒሁ፡ ለኑዛዜሆሙ፡ ወለተድላሆሙ፡ በርእየ፡ ዚአሁ፨ እስከ፡ ይረስዑ፡
                        ርእሶሙ፡ ወይሠጠሙ፡ ውስተ፡ ተደሞ፥ ዘባሕረ፡ አስተርእዮቱ፡ ብርሃናዊ፨ ቡሩክ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ ዘወሀበ፡ እሎንተ፡ በዝየ፡
                        ለጠባይዓቲነ፨ ሎቱ፡ ስብሐት፡ ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም፡ አሜን፡ ለይኩን፡ ለይኩን፨፨፨
                        <foreign xml:lang="en">This book was translated from the Arabic language into the new language Gǝʿǝz on the word of order of Lǝbna
                           Dǝngǝl the king <gap reason="ellipsis"/></foreign>
                        <note>The embedded colophon refers to the translation of the work in the time of King
                           <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6229LebnaDe">Lǝbna Dǝngǝl</persName> (<date type="reign" notBefore="1508" notAfter="1540"/>).
                           For other embedded colophons of ʾAragāwi Manfasāwi see: <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESgkm001">Gāntā ʾAfašum, Maḵodʿa Dabra Gannat Kidāna Mǝḥrat, GKM-001</ref>, <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESdd036">Bǝḥerāwi Kǝllǝlāwi Mangǝśti Tǝgrāy, Dabra Dāmmo ʾAbuna ʾAragāwi, C3-IV-251</ref> and <ref type="mss" corresp="https://betamasaheft.eu/ESmakm012">ʾƎndartā, Māy ʾAnbasā Dabra Gannat Kidāna Mǝḥrat, MAKM-012</ref>.</note>
                     </explicit>
                     
                     <colophon xml:id="coloph1">
                        <locus target="#149ra"/>
                        <quote xml:lang="gez">ዛቲ፡ መጽሐፍ፡ ተወጥነት፡ አመ፡ ፯ለታሕሣሥ፡ በዘመነ፡ ዮሐንስ፡
                        ወንጌላዊ፡ በ፸፻በ፩፻፶ወ፯፡ ዓመተ፡ ምሕረት፡ ወተፈጸመት፡ በ፳ወ፩፡ ሌሊትወበ፲ወ፯፡ መዓልት፡ ዘውእቱ፡ ወርኃ፡ የካቲት፡ ሎቱ፡
                        ስብሐት፨ ዘአጽሐፋሰ፡ በጻሕቅ፡ ኃጥእ፡ ወምስኪን፡ አባ፡ <hi rend="rubric">ሰፋኒ፡ ክርስቶስ፡</hi> ዘደብረ፡ ደሴተ፡ ሐይቅ፡ ወዘጸሐፋሂ፡ <hi rend="rubric">ገበረ፡
                        ድንግል፡</hi> ኅቡረ፡ ይምሐሮሙ፡ እግዚአብሔር፡ በመንግሥተ፡ ሰማያት፡ አሜን፨፨፨ </quote>
    
                        <quote xml:lang="en">This book was started on 7th of the month Tāḥśāś in the
                        year of St John the Evangelist in 7000 in 156 year of mercy and was completed
                        on the 21st night and 17th day of the month Yakkātit, glory to Him. The one who
                        commissioned it with eager is a sinner and poor ʾAbbā Safāni Krǝstos of the
                        Island on Lake Ḥayq and the one who wrote it is Gabra Dǝngǝl, let God have
                        mercy upon both of them in the Kingdom of Heaven, Amen.</quote> 
                        <note>
                       The colophon mentions the date of production, <date calendar="world" when-custom="7156" when="1664">7156 ‘years of mercy’ (should be ‘years of the world’) 
                          that is, 1664 A.D.</date>, as well as the commissioner <persName role="patron" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15397SafaniKr"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Safāni Krǝstos</persName> from 
                           <placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/INS0327DHE">Dabra Ḥayq ʾƎsṭifānos  (Dabra Daseta Ḥayq)</placeName> 
                           and the scribe <persName role="scribe" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15400GabraDengel">Gabra Dǝngǝl</persName>.</note>
                     </colophon>
                  </msItem>
                  
