                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">Second half of the seventeenth-century script.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>
                        <desc>Fine, careful and regular; the manuscript was copied by <persName role="scribe" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15400GabraDengel">Gabra Dǝngǝl</persName> (see <ref target="#coloph1"/> on <locus target="#149rb"/>).</desc>
                      
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; names of the owners and the scribe; the incipit page of <ref target="#ms_i1"/>, <ref target="#ms_i1.2"/> and <ref target="#ms_i1.4"/> (1st, 3rd and 5th lines);
                           elements of punctuation marks and Ethiopic numerals; the titles of homilies, epistles, letters, prayers and the petition;
                           three initial lines of the colophon.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
                  
                  <additions>
                     <list>
                        <item xml:id="a1">
                           <locus from="1ra" to="1va"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText">Unidentified prayer dedicated to Jesus Christ referring to His passion. The prayer is incomplete at the beginning.  
                              At the end of the text there is a brief supplication, asking for forgiveness of sins for <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15398SarsaYoh">Śarṣa Yoḥannǝs</persName>.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez"><gap reason="omitted"/> ያተ፡ እንግድዓከኒ፡ ቅንው፡ ምስለ፡ መስቀል፡ 
                              ዘ፩፡ ቀናት፡ ዘውፅአ፡ እንተ፡ ዘባንከ፡ አእጋሪከኒ፡ ቅንዋት፡ እንዘ፡ ያስተጣግዑ፡ ፩ደ፡ ምስለ፡ ካልኡ፡ <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a2">
                           <locus from="149va" to="150rb"/>
                           <desc type="GuestText"><title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT5627NagaraArestaAemro">Nagara ʾarʾǝsta ʾaʾǝmro</title>; it is written by a well-practised hand.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ለ፬ዘይቤ፡ ልባዌ፡ አንብቦ፡ ዝማሬ፡ ጣዕመ፡ ዝማሬ፨
                              ለ፫ዘይቤ፡ አንብዕ፡ ኵነኒ፡ ዑቃቢ፡ ፍቅረ፡ ደቂቀ፡ እጓለ፡ እምሕያው፡ ሁሰት። ወበውስቴቱ፡ ይትኀብኡ፡ ፫ዘይቤ፡
                              ንጽሐ፡ ሥጋ፡ ንጽሐ፡ ሕሊና፡ ንጽሮ። ምስለ፡ ፲ዘይቤ፡ እምልባዌ፡ እስከ፡ ከዊነ፡ እሳት <gap reason="ellipsis" resp="MK"/></q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a3">
                           <locus target="#150rb"/>
                           <desc type="PoemArke">An unidentified salām-hymn dedicated to <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5740JohnSab">ʾAragāwi Manfasāwi</persName>, written by a mediocre hand.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ሰላም፡ ለዮሐንስ፡ እምብዝኃ፡ አንክሮ፡ ወተደሞ፨
                              ነጽሮተ፡ ሥሉስ፡ ቅዱስ፡ ከመ፡ ማዕበለ፡ ባሕር፡ ዘያሠጥሞ፨ 
                              ሶበ፡ ኂርውናሁ፡ ነጸሩ፡ ወዘዚአሁ፡ አርምሞ፨
                              እንዘ፡ ውእቱ፡ ወሬዛ፡ ዘእንበለ፡ ያብጽሕ፡ ዓቅሞ፨ 
                              አረጋዊ፡ መንፈሳዊ፡ ሰመይዎ፡ ስሞ፨</q>
                           <quote xml:lang="en">
                             Hail to Yoḥannǝs from much of
                             admiration and wonder. Whom the vision of the Trinity submerged like a
                              wave of the sea. When they saw his benevolence and his quietness While
                              he was young and had not grown up yet He was called Spiritual
                              Elder.</quote>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a4">
                           <locus target="#150rb"/>
                           <desc type="Poem">An unidentified poem dedicated to <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS5740JohnSab">ʾAragāwi Manfasāwi</persName>, written by a mediocre hand.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">
                              ጳራቅሊጦስ፡ መንፈሰ፡ ትንቢት፡ ለናሆም፡ ዘሐወፆ፨
                              መጳራቅሊጦስ፡ መብረቅ፡ ለጳውሎስ፡ ዘአደንግፆ፨ መራኁተ፡ ስምዖን፡ ጴጥሮስ፡ ጳራ፡ ፈታሔ፡ ማዕፆ፨ ለአረጋዊ፡
                              መንፈሳዊ፡ ያርኅወኒ፡ አንቀጾ፨ ስብሐተ፡ መልክዑ፡ እነጽር፡ ወፍሡሐ፡ ገጾ፨</q>
                           <q xml:lang="en">
                             Paraclete, the Spirit of prophecy who visited Nāhom, Paraclete who terrified Paul with a
                              lightening, With the key of Simon Peter, the guardian of the gate,
                              Paraclete, May he open the gate for Spiritual Elder, So that I could
                              see his glorious appearance and his joyful face.</q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a5">
                           <locus from="150va" to="151rb"/>
                           <desc type="LandGrant">Register of land plots (?), in Amharic and Gǝʿǝz, in two parts.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="am"> አፄ፡ ሶሎሞን፡ የፋሲለደስ፡ የሰጡት፡ ኍልቁ፡
                              ምድር፡ ዘሀሎ፡ በጉንትር፡ ፮ ገመድ፡ የተክለ፡ ሳሙኤል፡ <gap reason="ellipsis"/></q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="a6">
                           <locus target="#151rb"/>
                           <desc type="OwnershipNote">A carelessly written ownership note of a much later provenance. 
                              It states that the owner of the book is <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15399Walda"><roleName type="title">ʾAbbā</roleName> Walda</persName> who received it from 
                              <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15401Hayla"><roleName type="title">ʾAbuna</roleName> Ḥāyla</persName>.</desc>
                           <q xml:lang="gez">ዛቲ፡ መጽሐፍ፡ ዘአባ፡ ወልደ፡ ዘወኃቦ፡ አቡነ፡ ኃይለ፡ ትሑት፡ የዋሕ፡ ወኄር፡ መፍቅሬ፡ ሰብ፡<sic/></q>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e1">
                           <desc>Amharic and Gǝʿǝz ʾandǝmtā-commentaries and glosses written in the margins throughout the text.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e2">
                           <desc>The introduction and homilies: 2, 7, 8, 15, as well as homily on <locus target="#57rb"/> contain a prayer distinguished from the main text with a
                              word <foreign xml:lang="gez">‘ṣalot’</foreign> in red ink. </desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e3">
                           <desc>Homily 17 contains parts called <foreign xml:lang="gez">ḥatatā</foreign> (‘question’) and <foreign xml:lang="gez">taśaṭwo</foreign> (‘answer’) written in red ink. </desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e4">
                           <locus target="#151v"/>
                           <desc>The Trinitarian formula with the beginning of <title ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LIT1978Mashaf">Maṣḥafa ṭomār</title>.</desc>
                        </item>
                        
                        <item xml:id="e5">
                           <desc>Writing exercises.</desc>
                        </item>
